// The owner ruled on the one question this toolchain was holding open, and the
// ruling is about shape rather than about a line in a compiler: a capsule's state
// changes through a method of that capsule, and every other method goes through
// that one. Nothing a method could be given to write directly is worth admitting,
// because a body that reaches for one is a body whose logic is written badly — and
// the endorsed shape needs nothing more than what [state.kh](./state.kh) already
// compiles, where the field reaches the method that writes it.
//
// So the call below is refused, and it is refused on purpose rather than held
// open: a call writes into a name the body binds, and whether a field is one of
// those names is a rule of this level and not a claim the documents make. The
// first call in the body is the same shape written on a name the body does bind,
// and it is what the second one would be if the field were a local.

tp Count cp {
}

tp Cursor cp {
    position Count
}

tp Next mt (self Cursor) (step Count) (moved Count) {
    return
}

tp Advance mt (self Cursor) (step Count) (moved Count) {
    vr local Count
    self.Next(local)(local)
    self.Next(local)(self.position)
}
